# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Red Chalk Across the Ridge Line

**Story & Context:** Before the first ridge-run performance, Malika draws a red chalk line across the veranda floor to mark the point where the city skyline disappears behind the hall wall. Sayan turns the line into a musical boundary: the igil remains on one open fifth until the percussion density crosses a predetermined threshold.

The track begins with frame drum, dry kick, and one narrow igil drone. Devon enters with clipped prepared-clavinet dyads on offbeats, while Anika holds a bass-oboe tone slightly above the sub root. Every eight bars, Malika adds one percussion voice until the groove becomes fully road-march driven. At the exact point of maximum density, Sayan shifts the drone for the first time.

The final section removes layers in reverse order, but the new drone remains, making the ending feel permanently altered despite returning to the original sparse texture.

